  "title": "Wildmarch",
  "tagline": "Everyone starts with a torch and a stick. The Wildmarch decides the rest.",
  "pitch": "An online third-person action RPG on one continent. You start in a farming valley with one spell and leave on foot. Every region north is harder, and almost everything that makes a character feel powerful — the dodge roll, the mount, your class's signature trick, talents, fast travel, the raid door — is earned by reaching a level or finishing an important quest. A sibling of Farhold: same Chibi 2 characters, items, perks, voices and combat feel, without the planet sandbox — plus other players, thirty bespoke class kits and boss fights you learn.",
  "pillars": [
    ["Earn every verb", "A new character is simple on purpose. The game gets bigger as you do."],
    ["Thirty classes, thirty kits", "No two classes share a spell. Each has one signature mechanic."],
    ["Readable danger", "Every attack that can kill you is telegraphed before it lands."],
    ["Bosses are the normal game", "Void zones, soaks, safe zones and talking bosses in the open world, dungeons and raids."],
    ["Loot worth talking about", "Class sets that change spells, legendaries that change play, secret-boss drops."],
    ["Together or alone", "Normal dungeons and all open-world content can be done solo with followers."]
